IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era-types`
IMPORT `era-dates`

-- Employment Relations Act 2000 — GOAL 1: TRIAL PERIODS AND HIGH EARNERS.
--
--   "Is the employee barred from bringing a grievance about the dismissal by
--    a trial provision or the remuneration threshold?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2000_24.txt — ss 67A, 67B,
-- 67I, 67J, 113A, 113B.

§ `Goal 1 — trial periods and high earners`

-- ss 67B(2)-(3), 113A(2)-(3): the bar covers a grievance under s 103(1)(a),
-- and under (b) if it relates to the dismissal; not (b) otherwise, nor (c) to
-- (k).
@ref ss 67B(2)-(3), 113A(2)-(3)
GIVEN g IS A Grievance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grievance is about the dismissal` g IF
        g's `ground` EQUALS `(a) unjustifiable dismissal`
    OR  (g's `ground` EQUALS `(b) unjustifiable disadvantage` AND g's `relates to the dismissal`)

-- s 67A "(1) An employment agreement containing a trial provision may be
-- entered into by an employer and an employee who has not previously been
-- employed by that employer. (2) ... trial provision means a written provision
-- ... that states ... that— (a) for a specified period (not exceeding 90
-- days), starting at the beginning of the employee's employment, the employee
-- is to serve a trial period". A period of n days starting on day S ends on
-- day S + n − 1.
@ref s 67A
GIVEN e IS AN Employment
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the trial period for` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e's `written trial provision for days`
    WHEN JUST n THEN
        IF   n AT MOST 90 AND NOT e's `previously employed by this employer`
        THEN JUST (`the day` (n MINUS 1) `days after` (e's `employment began on`))
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 67B "(1) This section applies if an employer terminates an employment
-- agreement containing a trial provision ... by giving the employee notice of
-- the termination before the end of the trial period, whether the
-- termination takes effect before, at, or after the end of the trial period.
-- (2) An employee whose employment agreement is terminated in accordance with
-- subsection (1) may not bring a personal grievance or legal proceedings in
-- respect of the dismissal".
@ref ss 67A, 67B(1)-(3)
GIVEN e IS AN Employment, g IS A Grievance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trial provision bars the grievance` e g IF
        `the grievance is about the dismissal` g
    AND (CONSIDER `the last day of the trial period for` e
         WHEN JUST last THEN e's `notice of termination given on` AT MOST last
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)

-- s 67I(4): "An employee's annual remuneration is calculated as follows"
-- (formula lost in the conversion; its items are the remuneration paid in the
-- 364 days and the days the employee held the position in them): read as
-- remuneration × 364 ÷ days held (fork F1).
@ref s 67I(4)
GIVEN e IS AN Employment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the annual remuneration of` e MEANS
    IF   e's `days held in the 364 days` AT MOST 0
    THEN `s 67I(4) needs at least one day in the position`
    ELSE e's `remuneration in the 364 days` TIMES 364 DIVIDED BY e's `days held in the 364 days`

`s 67I(4) needs at least one day in the position` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 67I(4): no days held in the position in the 364 days"

-- s 113A "(1) This section applies to an employee if— (a) the employee is
-- dismissed by their employer; and (b) the employee's annual remuneration
-- meets or exceeds the specified remuneration threshold. (2) The employee may
-- not bring a personal grievance or legal proceedings in respect of the
-- dismissal". s 67J: unless both agreed in writing that ss 67I and 113A do
-- not apply.
@ref ss 67J, 113A
GIVEN e IS AN Employment, g IS A Grievance
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remuneration threshold bars the grievance` e g IF
        `the grievance is about the dismissal` g
    AND NOT e's `agreed in writing that ss 67I and 113A do not apply`
    AND `the annual remuneration of` e AT LEAST e's `specified remuneration threshold`

@ref ss 67B, 113A
@export Whether a dismissed employee is barred from a personal grievance about the dismissal under the Employment Relations Act 2000 (NZ): by a written trial provision of up to 90 days for a new employee, if notice of termination was given before the trial ended (s 67B); or by annual remuneration at or above the specified threshold ($200,000, as increased), unless the parties agreed otherwise in writing (ss 67J, 113A). Grievances on other grounds, or about disadvantage unrelated to the dismissal, are not barred. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN Employment  @desc The start of employment, prior employment, any trial provision, the notice date, remuneration and days in the 364 days, the threshold, and any s 67J agreement
      g IS A Grievance  @desc The ground, and whether it relates to the dismissal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grievance is barred` e g IF
        `the trial provision bars the grievance` e g
    OR  `the remuneration threshold bars the grievance` e g

-- s 113B "(2) The specified remuneration threshold must increase in a given
-- year if the amount of average ordinary weekly earnings for the first quarter
-- of that year ... is more than the amount ... for the first quarter of the
-- year in which the specified remuneration threshold last increased ... (3)
-- ... increased by the percentage that results from the following formula"
-- (lost; read as (given − last) ÷ last × 100, fork F2) "(4) If the amount
-- that results from the percentage increase is not a whole number, it must be
-- rounded to the nearest whole number." A half rounds up (changed after
-- the independent pass: the language's ROUND rounds halves to even).
@ref s 113B(2)-(4)
GIVEN threshold IS A NUMBER, given IS A NUMBER, last IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the remuneration threshold from` threshold `, earnings this year` given `, in the year of last increase` last MEANS
    IF   given GREATER THAN last
    THEN FLOOR (threshold TIMES given DIVIDED BY last PLUS 0.5)
    ELSE threshold
